  "physical_validity": "Horizontal flips are plausible for many crack and pothole appearances but reverse traffic handedness and signs; retain only when these semantics are irrelevant. Mild HSV jitter approximates illumination changes, while extreme hue/saturation changes are unrealistic. Mosaic creates artificial seams and changes damage scale/context, so inspect its effect on small cracks. Vertical flips put road geometry upside down and are physically implausible for normal forward-facing road images; flipud remains zero. Validation and test images receive no training augmentation.",
